		class=&#34;gallery-image&#34; 
		data-flex-grow=&#34;133&#34;
		data-flex-basis=&#34;320px&#34;
	
&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Emsworthy Barn is the last remaining structure of Emsworthy Farm. It&amp;rsquo;s used now as an occasional store for conservation management equipment by the Devon Wildlife Trust who manage the nearby Emsworthy Mire. There is also an owl box inside.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The entire area is richly carpeted in Bluebells through April and May and draws thousands and thousands of visitors keen to experience the sight and improve their social media.  On the opposite side of the valley, Holwell Lawn also features a huge area of Bluebells and makes quite the spectacle when they&amp;rsquo;re in flower.&lt;/p&gt;
