&lt;h2 id=&#34;hemsworthy-quarries&#34;&gt;Hemsworthy Quarries
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Also known as Harrowbeer Quarry, Emsworthy East Quarry is one of five interconnected quarries comprising the Haytor Down quarry group, which was started by George Templer in 1813 and last worked in the 1840s, having passed to the Johnson Brothers who also quarried Foggintor and surrounding areas.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will cross various old tramways which once carried Granite from the smaller quarries to the main Haytor Quarry site for transport off the moor.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;http://localhost:1313/p/haytor-rocks-and-quarries/&#34; &gt;More information about the Haytor Quarries is available on our Haytor Quarry walk&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
